20.  * for a given file using last-match-wins semantics.
21.  *
22.  * <p>The service is intentionally listener-free: it reparses lazily when a
23.  * caller asks for rules and the cached document/file stamp has changed. The
24.  * widget owns its own VFS / PSI listeners and drives re-resolution; centralizing
25.  * cache-invalidation that way avoids a feedback loop between service and UI.
26.  *
27.  * <p>For a given file the service walks up its parent chain looking for
28.  * {@code .github/CODEOWNERS}, {@code CODEOWNERS}, {@code docs/CODEOWNERS}, and
29.  * {@code .gitlab/CODEOWNERS} (GitHub's documented precedence, plus the GitLab
30.  * location). The first hit wins, which makes monorepos with per-module
31.  * CODEOWNERS files behave the way {@code git} does and keeps the lookup
32.  * independent of how the project's content roots happen to be registered.
33.  */
34. @Service(Service.Level.PROJECT)
35. public final class CodeownersService {
36. 
37.   private static final String[] CANDIDATE_PATHS = {
38.           ".github/CODEOWNERS",
39.           "CODEOWNERS",
40.           "docs/CODEOWNERS",
41.           ".gitlab/CODEOWNERS",
42.   };
